  "worked_solution": "To find $\\frac{{\u2202}^{2}f}{\u2202y\u2202x}$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202x}$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\u2202}^{2}f}{\u2202y\u2202x} & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(2x{y}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =2x\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}({y}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =2x[2y\\cdot {e}^{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}+{y}^{2}\\cdot ({e}^{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\cdot 2y{x}^{2})] \\\\  & =4xy{e}^{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}+4{x}^{3}{y}^{3}{e}^{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =4xy(1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}){e}^{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
